--- PRE-EXISTING, OUT-OF-SCOPE BUILD BLOCKER (not introduced by this change) ----
The environment's Swift toolchain is Apple Swift 6.3.2 / Xcode 26 / MacOSX26.5 SDK — NEWER and
stricter than the toolchain this repo targets. The full TeslaSync app target does not compile in
this environment due to repo-wide PRE-EXISTING errors in files OUTSIDE this task's allowed scope:
  * 685 co-located *.Previews.swift files use #Preview idioms the new compiler rejects, e.g.
    TeslaSync/shared-surfaces/Input.Previews.swift:88  'cannot use explicit return in ViewBuilder'
    TeslaSync/shared-surfaces/Input.Previews.swift:94  'argument placeholder must precede error'
  * sibling PRODUCTION code, e.g.
    Sources/Features/Driving/DriveScorePage.Panels.swift:25
      'cannot convert LocalizedStringKey to String.LocalizationValue' (String(localized:) overload change)
  * macOS app/widget targets additionally require a development signing certificate (none in env).
These reproduce on a pristine tree (git shows Input.Previews.swift + project.yml UNMODIFIED by this
change) and affect every page's gate equally. They were NOT fixed: they are out of the allowed file
set (apps/apple/.../Features/Admin/**, nav registration, the string catalog, this log) and number in
the hundreds. To VERIFY my work despite this, *.Previews.swift were excluded only via the throwaway
xcodebuild override EXCLUDED_SOURCE_FILE_NAMES='*.Previews.swift' (never written to project.yml), and
my code was additionally compiled+run standalone (above). No out-of-scope file is modified in the deliverable.

